  "title": "Engine Orchestration \u0026 Workflow Engine Architecture",
  "traces": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "title": "LLMChatEngine: Tool-Calling Loop Execution",
      "description": "Agent engine system - core LLM execution loop that iteratively calls tools until completion",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "1a",
          "path": "internal/engine/llmchat_engine.go",
          "lineNumber": 116,
          "lineContent": "func (e *LLMChatEngine) Run(ctx context.Context, input EngineInput) (EngineOutput, error) {",
          "title": "Engine entry point",
          "description": "Main execution method implementing AgentEngine interface"
        },
        {
          "id": "1b",
          "path": "internal/engine/llmchat_engine.go",
          "lineNumber": 141,
          "lineContent": "\t\tresp, err := e.callLLM(ctx, messages, tools)",
          "title": "LLM API call",
          "description": "Sends messages and tool definitions to OpenAI-compatible API"
        },
        {
          "id": "1c",
          "path": "internal/engine/llmchat_engine.go",
          "lineNumber": 161,
          "lineContent": "\t\tif len(choice.Message.ToolCalls) \u003e 0 {",
          "title": "Tool call detection",
          "description": "Checks if LLM requested tool execution instead of final response"
        },
        {
          "id": "1d",
          "path": "internal/engine/llmchat_engine.go",
          "lineNumber": 177,
          "lineContent": "\t\t\t\tresult, _ = e.toolRunner.Execute(ctx, toolCall)",
          "title": "Tool execution",
          "description": "Delegates to ToolRunner which handles hooks and actual tool invocation"
        },
        {
          "id": "1e",
          "path": "internal/engine/llmchat_engine.go",
          "lineNumber": 188,
          "lineContent": "\t\t\t\tmessages = append(messages, oaiMessage{",
          "title": "Result appending",
          "description": "Adds tool result to conversation history for next iteration"
        },
        {
          "id": "1f",
          "path": "internal/engine/llmchat_engine.go",
          "lineNumber": 196,
          "lineContent": "\t\t\tcontinue",
          "title": "Loop continuation",
          "description": "Returns to top of loop for next LLM call with tool results"
        },
        {
          "id": "1g",
          "path": "internal/engine/llmchat_engine.go",
          "lineNumber": 200,
          "lineContent": "\t\toutput.AssistantText = choice.Message.Content",
          "title": "Final response",
          "description": "No tool calls means LLM provided final answer, exit loop"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "LLMChatEngine Tool-Calling Loop \u003c-- internal/engine/llmchat_engine.go:17\n├── Run() entry point \u003c-- 1a\n│   └── Main execution loop (for iteration) \u003c-- internal/engine/llmchat_engine.go:124\n│       ├── callLLM() API request \u003c-- 1b\n│       │   └── HTTP POST to OpenAI-compatible \u003c-- internal/engine/llmchat_engine.go:285\n│       ├── Response processing \u003c-- internal/engine/llmchat_engine.go:152\n│       │   └── Check for tool calls \u003c-- 1c\n│       ├── Tool execution branch (if tool calls) \u003c-- internal/engine/llmchat_engine.go:161\n│       │   ├── toolRunner.Execute() \u003c-- 1d\n│       │   │   └── Delegates to ToolRunner w/ hooks\n│       │   ├── Append tool result to messages \u003c-- 1e\n│       │   └── Loop continuation \u003c-- 1f\n│       └── Final response branch (no tool calls) \u003c-- internal/engine/llmchat_engine.go:199\n│           └── Extract assistant text \u003c-- 1g\n└── Return EngineOutput \u003c-- internal/engine/llmchat_engine.go:202",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nLLM agents need to **iteratively call tools** until they complete a task. When you ask an LLM to \"read file X and summarize it,\" the LLM can't directly access files—instead, it must request a `read_file` tool call, receive the result, then generate a summary. Complex tasks require **multiple rounds** of tool calls, where each result informs the next action. The `LLMChatEngine` implements this **agentic loop** using OpenAI-compatible APIs (OpenRouter, Groq, OpenAI, etc.).\n\n## Details\n\n### Core Loop Structure\n\nThe engine runs a **for loop** [1a] that continues until the LLM provides a final text response instead of requesting more tools. Each iteration:\n\n1. **Calls the LLM API** [1b] with the conversation history (user messages, assistant responses, tool results)\n2. **Checks the response** [1c] for tool calls in the message\n3. If tool calls exist, **executes each tool** [1d] via `ToolRunner` (which handles hook integration)\n4. **Appends tool results** [1e] to the conversation as new messages\n5. **Continues the loop** [1f] to call the LLM again with the updated context\n\n### Termination\n\nThe loop exits when the LLM returns a message **without tool calls** [1c], indicating it has enough information to provide a final answer. The engine then **extracts the assistant text** [1g] and returns it as the final output.\n\n### Tool Execution\n\nTool execution [1d] is delegated to `ToolRunner`, which wraps the actual tool call with **pre/post hooks** for observability, blocking, and input/output mutation. This separation allows the engine to focus on the LLM loop while hooks handle cross-cutting concerns like logging, security policies, and context injection.\n\n### API Compatibility\n\nThe engine uses **OpenAI's chat completions format** [1b], making it compatible with multiple providers. It constructs requests with messages, tool definitions, temperature, and max tokens, then parses responses to extract tool calls or final text."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "title": "AgentActor: Console Message to Engine Execution",
      "description": "Agent engine system - reactive actor handling console requests by routing to appropriate engine (LLMChat or DSPy)",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "2a",
          "path": "internal/actor/agent_actor.go",
          "lineNumber": 773,
          "lineContent": "func (a *AgentActor) handleConsoleAsk(ctx context.Context, msg *Message) (*Message, error) {",
          "title": "Message handler entry",
